ud7.10:4.1 | S: Then, understanding this matter, on that occasion the Buddha expressed this heartfelt sentiment: | T: Then, on realizing the significance of that, the Blessed One on that occasion exclaimed:
ud7.10:5.1 | S: “The world is caught up in delusion, | T: Bound round with delusion, the world
ud7.10:5.2 | S: but is looked on as making sense. | T: only appears to be competent.
ud7.10:5.3 | S: The fool caught up in attachment | T: Bound with acquisitions, foolish,
ud7.10:5.4 | S: is surrounded by darkness. | T: surrounded by darkness,
ud7.10:5.5 | S: It seems as if eternal, | T: it seems eternal,
ud7.10:5.6 | S: but for one who sees, there is nothing.” | T: but for one who sees, there is nothing.
ud7.10:5.7 | P: Dasamaṁ. | T: (none)
